# Operation authorization

```elixir
Mix.install([{:wardrik, "~> 0.1.0-rc.9"}, {:kino, "~> 0.19"}])
```

## An authorizer

Wardrik asks your authorizer before every operation. This one lets Maria do anything with her
agent, Jon read it, and Sam not see it. Agents can't forget agents. In a chat, only the owner or
whoever asked decides. Nothing here calls a model.

Maps stand in for your tables:

```elixir
defmodule MyApp.Authorizer do
  @behaviour Wardrik.Authorizer

  alias Wardrik.Authorizer.Request

  @teams %{"maria" => "acme", "jon" => "acme", "ana" => "acme", "sam" => "globex"}
  @owners %{"agt_books" => "maria", "agt_triage" => "maria"}

  # What anyone on the owner's team may do. The rest is the owner's.
  @shared ["agent.read", "agent.events", "agent.ask", "agent.decide"]

  @impl true
  def authorize(%Request{resource: {:agent, id}, principal: %{id: who}} = request, _opts) do
    owner = @owners[id]

    if owner && @teams[owner] == @teams[who],
      do: allowed(request, owner),
      else: {:error, :not_found}
  end

  def authorize(_request, _opts), do: {:error, :forbidden}

  defp allowed(%Request{actor: {:agent, _}, action: "agent.forget"}, _owner),
    do: {:error, :forbidden}

  defp allowed(%Request{actor: {:channel, _}, action: "agent.decide"} = request, owner) do
    if request.principal.id in [owner, request.context[:asked_by]],
      do: :ok,
      else: {:error, :forbidden}
  end

  defp allowed(%Request{action: action}, _owner) when action in @shared, do: :ok
  defp allowed(%Request{principal: %{id: owner}}, owner), do: :ok
  defp allowed(_request, _owner), do: {:error, :forbidden}
end

defmodule MyApp.Agents do
  @behaviour Wardrik.Resolver
  def resolve(_request, _opts), do: {:ok, %Wardrik.Resolved{principal: Wardrik.principal("maria")}}
end

{:ok, _} =
  Wardrik.start_link(
    name: MyApp.AgentRuntime,
    authorizer: {MyApp.Authorizer, []},
    resolver: {MyApp.Agents, []}
  )

maria = Wardrik.as(MyApp.AgentRuntime, "maria")
{:ok, _} = Wardrik.Agent.define(maria, "agt_books", model: "anthropic:claude-haiku-4-5")
```

- `:ok` - allowed.
- `{:error, :not_found}` - they can't see it, and learn nothing about it.
- `{:error, :forbidden}` - they see it, but may not do this.

## People

```elixir
jon = Wardrik.as(MyApp.AgentRuntime, "jon")
sam = Wardrik.as(MyApp.AgentRuntime, "sam")

tries = [
  read: &Wardrik.Agent.read(&1, "agt_books"),
  events: &Wardrik.Agent.events(&1, "agt_books"),
  stop: &Wardrik.Agent.stop(&1, "agt_books"),
  define: &Wardrik.Agent.define(&1, "agt_books", model: "anthropic:claude-haiku-4-5")
]

answer = fn
  {:error, %Wardrik.Error{type: type}} -> Atom.to_string(type)
  _ok -> "ok"
end

may = fn scopes ->
  for {name, scope} <- scopes do
    Map.new([{:who, name} | for({action, try} <- tries, do: {action, answer.(try.(scope))})])
  end
  |> Kino.DataTable.new(keys: [:who | Keyword.keys(tries)], name: "Who may do what")
end

may.(maria: maria, jon: jon, sam: sam)
```

Lists leave out what's refused:

```elixir
{Wardrik.Agents.list(jon), Wardrik.Agents.list(sam)}
```

## An agent

An agent's tools act for the person it works for, with `actor: {:agent, id}`:

```elixir
triage = Wardrik.as(MyApp.AgentRuntime, "maria", actor: {:agent, "agt_triage"})

answer.(Wardrik.Agent.forget(triage, "agt_books"))
```

## A chat member

The channel adds who asked. Here the scope is built by hand:

```elixir
deciding = fn member ->
  Wardrik.as(MyApp.AgentRuntime, member,
    actor: {:channel, "slack"},
    context: %{installation: %{owner: "acme", workspace: "T0123"}, asked_by: "jon"}
  )
end

for member <- ["jon", "maria", "ana"] do
  decides =
    Wardrik.Authorizer.authorize(deciding.(member),
      action: "agent.decide",
      resource: {:agent, "agt_books"}
    )

  %{who: member, decides: inspect(decides)}
end
|> Kino.DataTable.new(keys: [:who, :decides], name: "Who decides in Slack")
```

